@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus µTest++
@brief Topics related to the µTest++ Testing Framework.

@details
The @b µTest++ project is a **modern C++** library designed to provide
a **lightweight and efficient**, **macro free**, **TAP based** testing
framework, purpose-built for embedded systems development.

The **C++ API** is the primary interface for writing test suites and
test cases. It is centred on three classes: the `runner` drives the test
session, runs the suites, and collects the results; a `suite` groups test
cases, which it creates with `test()`; and a `test_case` evaluates the
expectations and the requirements. Function comparators
and logical functions complement the core API to enable expressive,
type-safe assertions with no macro dependencies. The API is documented in the
@ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api group.

The **command-line interface (CLI)** allows test executables to be
configured at run time without recompilation. Arguments are passed to
`runner::initialise()` and control aspects such as the verbosity level,
the output reporter format, the colours, an output file, and the
selection or listing of the test cases. The available options are documented in
the @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cli group.
